      <bioghist id="aspace_a7988683914e9fd1d41ac91f2bec64cc">
         <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
         <p>Roberto Sierra is an American composer. He studied at the University of Puerto Rico, the Conservatory of Puerto Rico, the Institute for Sonology in Utrecht, and the Hamburg Hochschule für Musik. In his music, Sierra combines European moderism with Latin American popular music and folk song.</p>
      </bioghist>
      <scopecontent id="aspace_15f9b2d5eb63cd7bb96f554ac9d66fd4">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>The Papers consist mainly of music and programs. Clippings, correspondence and other documents are also included. The collection should be considered partial, as Sierra is currently an active composer.</p>
      </scopecontent>
      <arrangement id="aspace_65b608f23035b6a86f1c10c4c6123d92">
         <head>Arrangement</head>
         <p>This is a minimally-processed collection; the Papers are divided loosely into five series: I. Music; II. Programs; III. Clippings; IV. Correspondence; and V. Contracts, Documents and Awards. Within these series, the collection remains unprocessed.</p>
      </arrangement>
